222
00:19:30,067 --> 00:19:30,860
Say, whole prayer.

223
00:19:31,103 --> 00:19:31,686
Whole prayer.

224
00:19:31,929 --> 00:19:32,657
I can't hear you.

225
00:19:32,722 --> 00:19:33,694
Say, whole prayer.

226
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:35,373
Whole prayer.

227
00:19:35,744 --> 00:19:35,987
Whole prayer.

228
00:19:36,148 --> 00:19:37,633
A supplication.

229
00:19:37,859 --> 00:19:38,279
A what?

230
00:19:38,408 --> 00:19:39,103
In the spirit.

231
00:19:41,160 --> 00:19:49,309
So one of the ministries of the Holy Spirit in your life is to supply all the aids that you need to pray.

232
00:19:49,614 --> 00:19:57,130
So God never expects you to pray any prayer outside the help of the Holy Spirit.

233
00:19:57,160 --> 00:20:03,420
The reason many Christians are struggling with prayer is because they do not have a conscious relationship.

234
00:20:03,560 --> 00:20:08,390
Now, whether you are conscious of the presence of the Holy Spirit or not, you have a relationship with him.

235
00:20:08,540 --> 00:20:17,260
But you need to have a conscious relationship with the Holy Spirit, and that is what we call the practice of God's presence.

236
00:20:18,980 --> 00:20:24,520
And one of the things the practice of the presence of the Holy Spirit does is this: it helps you to pray spontaneously.

237
00:20:25,887 --> 00:20:28,275
Do you know they asked Smith Wigglesworth?

238
00:20:29,333 --> 00:20:31,545
They said, sir, please tell us.

239
00:20:32,475 --> 00:20:33,726
How many of you know Smith Wigglesworth?

240
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:35,377
Praise God.

241
00:20:36,162 --> 00:20:39,416
I think we should be having criteria to admit people for hearing of faith.

242
00:20:40,106 --> 00:20:41,500
I don't know if you know Smith Wigglesworth.

243
00:20:41,693 --> 00:20:46,582
All right, now you hear the amazing things that God did through this man of God.

244
00:20:47,207 --> 00:20:48,073
Amazing things.

245
00:20:48,506 --> 00:20:51,471
He raises the dead as if he's waking people from sleep.

246
00:20:51,954 --> 00:20:59,806
Now they asked him, they said, please tell us your spirit, tell us, tell us your secrets, tell us your secrets.

247
00:21:00,196 --> 00:21:05,812
We know that this thing can never be possible without a robust prayer life.

248
00:21:06,218 --> 00:21:08,560
Tell us your prayer secrets.

249
00:21:09,768 --> 00:21:17,432
And he said that I have never prayed more than 30 minutes, I've never prayed more than 20 minutes at a time.

250
00:21:17,672 --> 00:21:25,383
In my life, but there is no 20 minutes that pass without me praying because there's no formula to this thing.

251
00:21:27,612 --> 00:21:36,238
Now, when we encourage you to do a minimum of 1 hour in tongues daily, it is to stretch, it is to exercise yourself.

252
00:21:37,146 --> 00:21:47,170
Because the thing is this: if you can do 1 hour praying in tongues on daily basis, it's just like you exercising, you are doing morning walk, morning jog, and all that.

253
00:21:48,120 --> 00:21:52,237
Now if they tell you that, hey, bandits is here, you have the stamina.

254
00:21:52,495 --> 00:21:56,160
And see, that you see danger does not mean that you have the strength to run.

255
00:21:56,916 --> 00:22:13,618
Yoruba has a saying that a 4-in-1 crippled man will not be a victim of war, because before the one will come close, he knows his condition.

256
00:22:14,098 --> 00:22:15,301
He would have vanished.

257
00:22:16,792 --> 00:22:17,253
Amen.

258
00:22:18,011 --> 00:22:18,834
Praise God forevermore.

259
00:22:20,140 --> 00:22:21,786
So you must learn to find your rhythm.

260
00:22:22,512 --> 00:22:25,611
He said, I have never prayed for more than 20 minutes.

261
00:22:27,260 --> 00:22:34,487
So if he says he has never prayed for more than 20 minutes, that at a stretch he prays under most 20 minutes.

262
00:22:35,457 --> 00:22:37,171
Look at the great things that God did with him.

263
00:22:39,772 --> 00:22:42,400
Oh, pastor is saying that I cannot reduce my prayer to 20 minutes.

264
00:22:42,482 --> 00:22:43,320
That's your cup of tea.

265
00:22:46,450 --> 00:22:46,934
Praise God.

266
00:22:47,516 --> 00:23:04,665
You know, I, I remember when I just started out in ministry, and then I, I devoured— oh my God, I, I've read virtually everything that Kenneth Hagin ever wrote, including manuscripts that didn't go into publication.

267
00:23:07,434 --> 00:23:15,333
And then I stumbled on one of his books, and when he said that he has never fasted for more than 3 days, I was angry.

268
00:23:16,106 --> 00:23:17,652
That God, are you a racist?

269
00:23:18,279 --> 00:23:21,870
Why is it that this thing is so easy for this Oyinbo people but for us?

270
00:23:22,224 --> 00:23:31,146
See, at that moment I began to pay more attention to Oyinbo minister, because if you listen to an African pastor, they just make this thing to look so lofty you cannot attain it.

271
00:23:32,157 --> 00:23:33,619
It is spiritual elitism.

272
00:23:34,431 --> 00:23:38,979
You know Jesus said that greater works than me— thank God that it was not an African man.

273
00:23:39,044 --> 00:23:40,016
Jesus was not an African man.

274
00:23:41,548 --> 00:23:42,580
You want to raise the dead?

275
00:23:42,837 --> 00:23:43,402
You know what?

276
00:23:43,482 --> 00:23:44,240
You know this thing now?

277
00:23:45,175 --> 00:23:46,159
You want to raise the dead?

278
00:23:49,160 --> 00:23:54,987
Ah, you will need to first do 12 hours, 6 months at stretch.

279
00:23:56,675 --> 00:23:58,603
Then you had midnight to eat.

280
00:23:59,544 --> 00:24:00,961
Then by then we know that you are ready.

281
00:24:02,105 --> 00:24:05,665
You can't hear those— how many people have been able to see?

282
00:24:05,826 --> 00:24:12,604
You can never— you can never motivate God's people to do God's will by fear.

283
00:24:14,130 --> 00:24:18,009
So in the days of thy power, thy people shall be willing.

284
00:24:19,334 --> 00:24:21,322
And then I read Benny Hinn.

285
00:24:21,662 --> 00:24:23,375
Benny Hinn said almost the same thing.

286
00:24:23,779 --> 00:24:26,918
I think he just said that he has never done more than 3 hours.

287
00:24:27,989 --> 00:24:29,157
Did these people do it?

288
00:24:29,222 --> 00:24:31,315
Is it that God have different standard for us in Africa?

289
00:24:32,050 --> 00:24:35,766
Because the story that me I hear from— you have to do 40 days.

290
00:24:36,202 --> 00:24:41,855
I, I attended— I think that the max marathon I've done is 21, above 21.

291
00:24:42,726 --> 00:24:43,065
Praise God.

292
00:24:43,210 --> 00:24:45,613
I wanted to do 40, but I had God.

293
00:24:46,291 --> 00:24:56,232
How many of you have locked yourself up in the room and say that God 'If you don't appear to me, I will die.' I've said it many times and I came out alive.

294
00:24:58,190 --> 00:25:01,304
Nobody will tell you, you'll be the one that will.

295
00:25:03,891 --> 00:25:04,279
Amen.

296
00:25:05,672 --> 00:25:06,336
Glory to God.

297
00:25:06,838 --> 00:25:08,086
So what am I saying?

298
00:25:10,210 --> 00:25:19,542
Whatever the level you have presently, one thing you must do away with to rise up on the wings of the Spirit is condemnation.

299
00:25:22,060 --> 00:25:24,948
And then find your rhythm in prayer.

300
00:25:26,077 --> 00:25:33,880
Because one thing that many people don't understand is this, you know, God said that he gives the spirit of grace and supplication.

301
00:25:34,734 --> 00:25:36,329
See, these things are in measures though.

302
00:25:38,180 --> 00:25:47,948
There are some people that the assignment, what God wants to use them for, for example, you have table knife Then you have kitchen knife.

303
00:25:49,056 --> 00:25:51,256
Then there is the one that butchers use.

304
00:25:52,123 --> 00:25:54,387
Then there are those that doctors use.

305
00:25:55,399 --> 00:25:57,213
Different degree of sharpness.

306
00:25:58,449 --> 00:26:10,315
Now there are some people, because of the kind of assignment that God have for Apostle Ayo Babalola, there is a certain dimension of engine that God puts on the inside of him that you don't need.

307
00:26:12,484 --> 00:26:16,005
Those are those here in the realm of the spirit, they are bulldozers.

308
00:26:17,717 --> 00:26:18,751
You know what they call dozers?

309
00:26:18,864 --> 00:26:19,962
They are bulldozers.

310
00:26:20,317 --> 00:26:23,379
Their assignment is to uproot Iroko trees.

311
00:26:25,740 --> 00:26:31,254
Now you that your assignment is to wither the small, small grass, your own one is not less important in the kingdom.

312
00:26:31,899 --> 00:26:37,948
You say, ah, Apostle Ayobabala, this man, and really that man has a very strong prayer life.

313
00:26:38,190 --> 00:26:44,239
Imagine they hand over a microphone to you for you to just close close a prayer meeting and then you close it for 3 days.

314
00:26:44,758 --> 00:26:45,570
That's not normal.

315
00:26:47,562 --> 00:26:47,934
Amen.

316
00:26:49,666 --> 00:26:50,394
Praise God.

317
00:26:51,122 --> 00:26:54,569
But you, you can't cook such thing up.

318
00:26:56,210 --> 00:26:58,501
You will have to be energized by a spirit.

319
00:26:59,695 --> 00:27:01,196
The same thing is applicable to fasting.

320
00:27:01,615 --> 00:27:06,864
Every single time people did 40 days fasting in scripture, it was not out of sheer will.

321
00:27:06,948 --> 00:27:08,278
It is not a formula.

322
00:27:08,682 --> 00:27:12,126
They were done with it, and then they realized that they have done 40 days.

323
00:27:14,340 --> 00:27:18,441
Because God will have to release the spirit of grace and supplication.

324
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:20,768
Are you following what I'm saying?

325
00:27:21,447 --> 00:27:23,806
So he says, all prayer— say after me, say all prayer.

326
00:27:24,759 --> 00:27:36,929
L say all prayer and supplication in the spirit, in the spirit, watching thereunto with all perseverance and supplication for all saints.

327
00:27:37,524 --> 00:27:47,862
So the reason we encourage you to have certain hours of prayer, on the minimum you pray daily, is for you to maximize what you have in Christ Jesus.

328
00:27:49,853 --> 00:27:58,339
It is for you to exercise yourself in the things of the spirit, because the matter will come up that will require you to tarry in the place of prayer.

329
00:27:58,532 --> 00:28:07,113
If you have not exercised yourself consistently on daily basis, you will not— if you stained in the days of adversity, your strength is small.

330
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:12,682
So all of this is just to build a system that will enable you to grow.

331
00:28:13,446 --> 00:28:14,426
Praise God forevermore.

332
00:28:16,390 --> 00:28:24,573
Jude 20 says, but ye, beloved, building up yourselves on your most holy faith, praying in what?

333
00:28:24,767 --> 00:28:25,381
In the flesh?

334
00:28:26,770 --> 00:28:27,712
In the Holy Ghost.

335
00:28:27,894 --> 00:28:34,861
So you see that every time God talks about prayer in his word, it is with the aid of the Spirit.

336
00:28:35,974 --> 00:28:41,487
Now, when you are not conscious of the ministry of the Holy Spirit, then you struggle.

337
00:28:42,810 --> 00:28:54,676
Now, my point is that prayer, right from the Old Testament, when God promised the Spirit, he let us understand that he is going to come with the Spirit of grace and supplication.

338
00:28:56,115 --> 00:29:00,088
You see it in 1 Corinthians chapter 14.

339
00:29:00,556 --> 00:29:01,363
Glory to God.

340
00:29:01,848 --> 00:29:02,849
It says, now what is it then?

341
00:29:03,059 --> 00:29:09,475
How we pray with the Spirit and how we pray with understanding also.

342
00:29:09,830 --> 00:29:11,722
When you are praying with the Spirit, what is going on?

343
00:29:11,802 --> 00:29:16,473
It is the Holy Spirit supplying utterance, supplying utterance.

344
00:29:17,328 --> 00:29:19,958
Praise God, praise God.

345
00:29:21,547 --> 00:29:29,741
So all the scriptures shows us one thing, that God never expect you to have a prayer life.

346
00:29:30,802 --> 00:29:38,289
In fact, he does not expect you to have a prayer moment outside the help of the Holy Spirit.

347
00:29:39,623 --> 00:29:46,966
So what I want to teach you this evening is how to respond to the help of the Holy Spirit.

348
00:29:48,329 --> 00:29:49,355
How to respond.

349
00:29:49,713 --> 00:30:05,053
You can learn all kinds of prayer, you can listen to all teachings, but if you do not know how to respond to the Spirit of grace and supplication, you will still not have a prayer life.

350
00:30:06,720 --> 00:30:09,382
Holy Spirit enables us to pray.

351
00:30:10,389 --> 00:30:25,437
Two things God said In that verse, he said, 'They will give you the spirit of one grace,' and then supplication.

352
00:30:26,500 --> 00:30:30,946
This grace is an enablement of the Holy Spirit.

353
00:30:34,300 --> 00:30:35,025
Then supplication.

354
00:30:35,073 --> 00:30:36,008
Now, what is supplication?

355
00:30:36,363 --> 00:30:39,635
Supplication is an earnest petition.

356
00:30:41,061 --> 00:30:42,593
Need to God.

357
00:30:43,319 --> 00:30:56,369
Supplication, it's emphasizing the earnest, the fervency with which you make your petition known to God.

358
00:30:57,384 --> 00:30:58,169
Glory to God!

359
00:30:58,922 --> 00:31:03,027
Heartfelt, heartfelt requests.

360
00:31:05,697 --> 00:31:06,748
Glory to God!

361
00:31:07,777 --> 00:31:09,567
Asu vele menoko sovai.

362
00:31:10,615 --> 00:31:13,227
Grandoku sovele mangladike tsuzuvai.

363
00:31:13,904 --> 00:31:24,605
You see, you, you can pray, you can pray for let's say maybe 10 minutes and generate more results than you pray for 1 hour.

364
00:31:24,670 --> 00:31:27,947
What makes the difference is how earnest the prayer is.

365
00:31:29,591 --> 00:31:36,693
I think I once thought on this when God sent Isaiah to tell Hezekiah that he should pack up, he's going to die.

366
00:31:36,741 --> 00:31:43,754
And Bible says that Ezekiel turned to the wall and he didn't pray in tongues.

367
00:31:45,820 --> 00:31:46,670
He didn't pray in tongues.

368
00:31:48,160 --> 00:31:50,042
He just— he just— that is petition.

369
00:31:51,138 --> 00:31:52,939
Petition is a specific request.

370
00:31:55,356 --> 00:31:56,492
It's a specific request.

371
00:31:58,818 --> 00:32:12,098
That specific request that you have, that, oh God, I know one of the reasons why I— and God forbid that you end this year without the prophecy of the dream year not being fulfilled in your life.

372
00:32:13,590 --> 00:32:16,148
Because see, dream year is not a petition.

373
00:32:16,760 --> 00:32:21,716
There must be something specific that reflects the dream prophecy.

374
00:32:22,970 --> 00:32:25,698
If the prayer is vague, it is not a petition.

375
00:32:28,341 --> 00:32:37,450
Now, for those who have written petition to maybe the police before, you know you have to be specific on what you are writing petition.

376
00:32:38,300 --> 00:32:47,762
Or somebody is trying to claim your land, then you will have to— in that petition, you have to state where the land is located, when you bought the land.

377
00:32:48,387 --> 00:32:54,650
You will attach documents that prove that you are the rightful owner of the property.

378
00:32:56,042 --> 00:33:07,331
Then you have to talk about what they are doing to the land and the specific thing you want the government to intervene on.

379
00:33:07,686 --> 00:33:08,508
Is that very clear?

380
00:33:08,734 --> 00:33:09,508
That is petition.

381
00:33:11,540 --> 00:33:18,558
You know, interestingly, you know, uh, you know, uh, Paul was writing to the church, said, see, be anxious for nothing.

382
00:33:20,796 --> 00:33:22,675
He said, but with what?

383
00:33:23,469 --> 00:33:32,884
Prayer and supplication, with thanksgiving, make your petition known unto God.

384
00:33:34,931 --> 00:33:36,367
So there must be specificity.

385
00:33:37,125 --> 00:33:38,385
That is what makes it a petition.

386
00:33:39,385 --> 00:33:40,209
Father, bless me.

387
00:33:40,273 --> 00:33:41,097
That's no petition.

388
00:33:43,872 --> 00:33:44,634
Is that very clear?

389
00:33:45,057 --> 00:33:48,954
Oh, do you know that the gift of the Holy Ghost is the blessing of Abraham?

390
00:33:49,665 --> 00:33:52,850
Oh, you didn't know that?

391
00:33:52,915 --> 00:33:59,435
We will receive the blessing of Abraham, which is the Holy Spirit.

392
00:34:00,913 --> 00:34:02,006
Healing is a blessing.

393
00:34:02,199 --> 00:34:02,857
Are you still there?

394
00:34:03,163 --> 00:34:10,652
He said all spiritual blessings in the heavenly places, but in petition you've got to be specific.

395
00:34:12,545 --> 00:34:20,932
And you see, the reason many people pray a prayer that is not heartfelt is because there is no specificity on that prayer.

396
00:34:21,245 --> 00:34:22,300
That's why you press.

397
00:34:24,102 --> 00:34:24,842
Brodo koso bi hai.

398
00:34:26,354 --> 00:34:31,749
Father, as I go out today, bless me, bless me, bless me, bless me, bless me, bless me.

399
00:34:33,196 --> 00:34:33,310
How?

400
00:34:34,742 --> 00:34:36,059
He has already blessed you.

401
00:34:36,973 --> 00:34:37,551
Isn't it?

402
00:34:38,963 --> 00:34:42,719
So a prayer for blessing is not a petition.

403
00:34:43,136 --> 00:34:49,541
He has already blessed you with all spiritual blessings in the heavenly places.

404
00:34:50,632 --> 00:34:55,752
So when you just say, Father, bless me, you are actually asking for what he has already done.

405
00:34:56,619 --> 00:35:01,194
But now you want an outworking of that blessing in your life.

406
00:35:02,012 --> 00:35:04,484
Oh Father, bless my family with a new house.

407
00:35:05,624 --> 00:35:08,787
We desire a 5-bedroom duplex.

408
00:35:09,558 --> 00:35:10,570
That is petition.

409
00:35:11,549 --> 00:35:12,256
That is petition.

410
00:35:12,850 --> 00:35:14,151
Oh, thank you, Lord Jesus.

411
00:35:14,681 --> 00:35:21,457
You've been writing application, you are not getting a favorable response, and you tabled the matter before the Lord.

412
00:35:21,826 --> 00:35:22,597
That is petition.

413
00:35:23,352 --> 00:35:28,635
And one thing about petition is this: you stay on it until you receive an answer of peace.

414
00:35:29,646 --> 00:35:37,546
So petition is the specific request The heartfelt prayer you pray regarding those things is the supplication.

415
00:35:37,916 --> 00:35:38,703
Is that very clear?

416
00:35:39,602 --> 00:35:43,038
So you cannot actually separate supplication from what?

417
00:35:43,407 --> 00:35:44,130
From petition.

418
00:35:44,804 --> 00:35:49,139
So supplication is how you pray.

419
00:35:50,584 --> 00:35:55,128
It is the intensity with which you present your case before the Lord.

420
00:35:55,321 --> 00:35:56,188
Glory to God!

421
00:35:56,606 --> 00:35:57,858
Thank you, Holy Spirit!

422
00:35:59,295 --> 00:36:00,735
Thank you, Holy Spirit.

423
00:36:02,339 --> 00:36:03,534
Thank you, Holy Spirit.

424
00:36:05,700 --> 00:36:07,398
I want to just repeat this again.

425
00:36:07,818 --> 00:36:17,979
God never intend, design prayer to be offered without the help of the Holy Spirit.

426
00:36:19,043 --> 00:36:20,815
But are you yielding to this help?

427
00:36:22,184 --> 00:36:23,698
Are you yielding to the Holy Spirit?

428
00:36:24,236 --> 00:36:32,511
That's why I say you, you must never leave your day without conscious awareness of the presence of the Holy Spirit.

429
00:36:33,377 --> 00:36:36,456
There's something about awareness, it makes you to respond.

430
00:36:37,081 --> 00:36:44,378
Now you, you can be in a house, you can be in a room with a snake, as long as you don't know, you won't react to it.

431
00:36:45,805 --> 00:36:50,199
I remember many years ago, I was— my mom told me to go get something.

432
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:53,059
From a particular spot in the room.

433
00:36:53,691 --> 00:36:59,456
And as I lifted the basket, I saw a snake coiled under the basket.

434
00:36:59,859 --> 00:37:00,666
I bolted.

435
00:37:02,618 --> 00:37:10,871
So the, the man that came to kill the snake, he said, from the look of things, this snake has actually been here for a very long time, but we never knew.

436
00:37:12,118 --> 00:37:15,454
The same thing is applicable to the things of the spirit.

437
00:37:15,777 --> 00:37:18,790
When you are not conscious of of it, you cannot respond to it.

438
00:37:19,372 --> 00:37:24,530
Some of you thought that you are prayerless, you don't, you don't have a passion for prayer.

439
00:37:24,627 --> 00:37:25,452
It is not true.

440
00:37:27,840 --> 00:37:32,223
You have— he says he has given you the Spirit whereby you cry.

441
00:37:32,465 --> 00:37:34,544
So it means you can't cry without the Spirit.

442
00:37:35,392 --> 00:37:38,407
Maybe I should run you through how the Holy Spirit helps you in prayer.

443
00:37:38,778 --> 00:37:41,810
I taught on this last year during, uh, Rivers Camp Meeting.

444
00:37:42,229 --> 00:37:42,907
Glory to God.

445
00:37:43,549 --> 00:37:49,701
The first thing the Holy Spirit helps you on in prayer is to prompt you to pray.

446
00:37:50,329 --> 00:37:50,909
Praise God!

447
00:37:51,376 --> 00:37:53,483
The Holy Spirit prompts you to pray.

